    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d774">

                <pb facs="0988" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg874"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860m.01/141</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Whitehouse</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August 24,
                        1922</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 8.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2266</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram No. 271, June
                    30, 1922, the Department’s telegraphic circular instruction of August 3 and my
                    despatches No. 2148 of July 21 and No. 2232 of August 17,<anchor n="87"
                        xml:id="d774-f1"/> all relative to the recognition of Lithuania, I have the
                    honor to forward herewith copy of a letter from the Lithuanian Legation, dated
                    August 4,<anchor n="88" xml:id="d774-f2"/> received to-day from the Secretariat
                    General of the Conference of Ambassadors.</p>
                <p>It appears from this letter that two questions may eventually come before the
                    Conference of Ambassadors: first, whether or not the Principal Allied Powers are
                    willing to accede to the Lithuanian interpretation of its obligations with
                    respect to the internationalization of the River Niemen—obligations which the
                    Principal Allied Powers made a condition precedent to their recognition <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de jure</hi> of Lithuania (see my despatch No. 2232);
                    second, the disposition to be made of the Territory of Memel.</p>
                <pb facs="0989" n="875" xml:id="pg875"/>
                <p>I should appreciate it if the Department would instruct me, in case one or both
                    of these questions should come before the Conference, whether it has any views
                    which it wishes presented, or whether I am to abstain from participation in any
                    discussion which may be had.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon
                    Whitehouse</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
